Rules: thresholds and the decision table
W H E N I S A S E N S O R H I G H ?
Sensor Reading High when
MQ-2 smoke 0 to 1023 above 400
IR flame 0 to 1023 (bigger = more 
flame) above 300
DHT11 temperature degrees C above 45
These are starting values. We calibrate them on our own sensors: 
record normal readings, then set each limit clearly above the 
normal maximum.
T H E D E C I S I O N R UL E
Sensors high Level Response
0 SAFE Green LED on
1 WARNING Yellow LED on
2 POSSIBLE FIRE Yellow blinks, slow beeps
3 FIRE DETECTED Red LED, buzzer, fan on
level = number of sensors that are high
Why: one sensor alone can be fooled by cooking smoke, strong sunlight or a hot room. Two or three agreeing is far more likely to be a real fire.
