Flowchart 1: the Python main loop
START open the serial port → load the settings → wait for the MQ-2 warm-up (120 s) → repeat the loop below
1 Read a line from the 
Arduino 2 Line valid? 3 Smooth the readings (average of 5)
4 Compare each sensor 
with its limit
No: skip the line. 5 bad lines in a row: 
SENSOR FAULT
5 Count the sensors that 
are high: level 0 to 3
6 Hold rule: level falls only 
after 10 s
7 Plan the outputs: LEDs, 
buzzer, fan, LCD
8 Send the command, print 
and log
repeat every second
While the MQ-2 is warming up, the loop only reads, shows WARMING UP and skips steps 3 to 8.
